{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Aḥor, tzartani</b> — from the root of וצרת עליה. Do not wonder that he did not say צרת עלי, for behold, similar to it is אל תצורם ואל תתגר בם." "<b>And the word vaqadam</b> — 'before' [i.e., in front]." "<b>Va'ahor</b> — the opposite of a person's forward motion. And the meaning is: for You pressed me behind and before, and You set upon me Your palm, and there is no siege and strait like this."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 139, :notes {0 "Resolved the root citation as Numbers 6:23; Ibn Ezra's argument depends on the verb צָרַר meaning 'to besiege/press'."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:42:08.952086898Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}